  "caption_final": "Ramayana: Rise of a Legend, Part 1 of Nitesh Tiwari's two-film Ramayana, has crossed ₹1,000 crore at the worldwide box office in its first eight days in cinemas, to Thursday 12 November. Trade tracker Sacnilk estimates its worldwide gross at ₹1,033.55 crore.\n\nThat is ₹675.05 crore gross from India and about ₹358.5 crore from overseas, which Sacnilk calls a rough estimate. India net collections stand at ₹564.6 crore. The makers have not confirmed these figures.\n\nIt is the 11th Indian film to pass ₹1,000 crore worldwide, and the third-fastest. Only Pushpa 2: The Rule and Dhurandhar: The Revenge got there within a week; Baahubali 2 took 10 days and RRR 16.\n\nDid you watch Ramayana in 3D or 2D, or are you still planning to see it?\n\nSources: Sacnilk, ETV Bharat, BizAsia, Film Companion\n\n#Ramayana #RamayanaPart1 #BoxOffice #IndianCinema #idlynerd\n\nImage: ReDefine (Prime Focus)",
